    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 212\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 2394, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the state finance law and the general municipal\n      law, in relation to payment in construction contracts\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend the provisions of the State Finance Law and  the\nGeneral   Municipal   law  to  expand  the  definition  of  \"substantial\ncompletion\" as it relates to construction contracts.\n \n  The bill would require that substantial completion be deemed to  occur\n\"when  the work required by the contract with the public owner is suffi-\nciently complete in accordance with the  contract  so  that  the  public\nowner  may  occupy  or  utilize the work for its intended use.\" The bill\ndoes not account for the fact that even after a project may be occupied,\nadditional work may be required before  the  project  is  deemed  to  be\nsubstantially complete.\n \n  Releasing contractors from this requirement will hamper the ability of\nboth  state  and  local  agencies  to  compel  contractors  to  complete\nconstruction projects if the project is deemed complete and retainage is\nreleased in this manner. Withholding a  modest  retainage  has  been  an\neffective  tool  and  financial  incentive  to  ensure  that contractors\ncomplete work as required under the terms of the contract.  The  failure\nto  include  such  requirements will lead to increased project costs and\ndelays to the  detriment  of  these  governmental  entities.  For  these\nreasons, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
